# Smart memory + low-VRAM generation (Tesla T4: 16GB VRAM / 16GB RAM)

Goal: make Z-Image Turbo run on a 16GB/16GB Tesla T4 that OOMs full-precision-resident.
Opt-in via `./webui.sh --smart-memory`. All changes are in the working tree, UNCOMMITTED.

## DONE (implemented, tested — 183 core tests pass, lint/pyright clean)

- [x] Smart-memory mode, opt-in: `webui.sh --smart-memory` -> INLINE_SMART_MEMORY=1
      (forces lowvram profile + sets PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True).
- [x] int8 quantization of the big weights (transformer + text encoder) via torchao
      weight-only (`Int8WeightOnlyConfig`). VAE stays full precision. Best-effort: a
      missing/incompatible torchao logs and falls back to full precision, never crashes.
      torchao added to the `zimage` extra (pyproject) and auto-installed at launch by webui.sh.
- [x] CRITICAL: int8 weights are kept RESIDENT on the GPU — NOT offloaded. torchao int8 +
      accelerate `enable_model_cpu_offload` DEADLOCK together (this was the "stuck after
      Read weights from disk" hang). Only a GPU too small for even int8-resident falls back
      to unquantized SEQUENTIAL offload.
- [x] #1 fp16 on Turing/Volta (compute capability < 8.0, e.g. T4): denoiser + text encoder
      run fp16 (uses the fp16 tensor cores); VAE stays upcast (fp32 when denoiser is fp16)
      to avoid black/NaN decode. bf16 kept on Ampere+.
- [x] #2 Clean CUDA-OOM message (points at --smart-memory / lower resolution), no raw traceback.
- [x] #3 `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` between runs + on OOM (curbs fragmentation, keeps model).
- [x] #5 Peak VRAM surfaced: reset/read per run, shown in the log AND the UI save status.
- [x] Renderer: Moodboard SideMenu (Assets/Outputs/Timeline rail) starts collapsed by default.

T4 now resolves to: denoiser fp16 / text-encoder fp16 / VAE fp32, int8, resident, no offload.

## NEXT (to verify / decide when continuing)

